        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Who is Iran's Chief negotiator Ghalibaf? Middle East Issued on: 11/04/2026 - 13:34 Modified: 11/04/2026 - 13:41 The 70-member Iranian delegation taking part in negotiations in Pakistan today is being led by one of Tehran’s most prominent non-clerical figures, Iranian Parliament Speaker Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf. Caroline Baum takes a look at the man Iran has entrusted with securing an end to the war on terms acceptable to Tehran. US, Iran sit down for talks in Islamabad 11/04/2026 Americas Israel refuses ceasefire with Hezbollah 11/04/2026 Middle East Iran, US delegations to start negotiations in Pakistan 11/04/2026 Americas 'Iran has put up a demand that Lebanon should be included in the ceasefire' 11/04/2026 Middle East Relentless airstrikes on Beirut's residential areas 'remind Lebanese that Israel is enemy as well' 10/04/2026 Middle East Pakistan plays major role trying to mediate an end to Iran war 09/04/2026 Middle East Netanyahu fails to address Israel’s failure to achieve war goals in Iran 09/04/2026 Middle East ‘Collective punishment’: At least 182 killed in Israeli strikes on Lebanon 08/04/2026 Middle East 'Pakistani military calling the shots: Has connections with IRCG, very good relationship with Trump' 08/04/2026 Middle East"
